SUMMARY:Parish Potluck Celebration
DESCRIPTION:In Honor of America’s 250th\nJoin us for a grand celebration of our parish’s history! There will be fun activities for all ages\, including a scavenger hunt and appearances by historic Saint James parishioners. We will also have several baked goods available for sampling from the cookbook of Mary Ross\, the great-granddaughter of George Ross\, a signer of the Declaration of Independence. Mary must have enjoyed potluck dinners; last year\, one of her descendants gifted Mary’s recipe book to Saint James. It includes not only her family recipes from the colonial era but also those she collected from other parishioners. \nCome and try some of her baking at our 250th Anniversary Potluck\, recreated by our bakers of history. \nClick here to let us know you’ll be attending. \nClick here to let us know what dish you’ll be bringing in Signup Genius.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/parish-potluck-celebration/
LOCATION:Saint James Parish House Forum Room\, 119 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
